{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-15T04:04:46.607Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-15T04:04:46.607Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-15T04:04:46.606Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Recurrence 2026-11-15 around 03:20Z, during local merge verification of PR #1732: the WAN uplink was saturated (ping RTT 1.2-2.7 s, TCP connect 3-14 s), so pnpm audit exceeded the collector's 60 s bound and OSV querybatch the 15 s per-batch bound. The receipt again recorded only status unavailable for both feeds, with no reason code, so telling a slow-but-reachable network from an outage took manual curl and ping probes. Because repository-static-quality also declares repository-dependency-advisories-required, the advisory verdict blocked the whole static assurance gate, and the merge proceeded on pinned evidence instead (lockfile identical to main, 0 Dependabot alerts, a hosted pass on the same lockfile). A bounded reason code (connect_timeout vs deadline_exceeded vs http_status) would have made that call immediate. Related: pm-amy32s (local merge evidence)."}]}],"before_hash":"569b9001ca28fcf4bd9c3a6cb257fdcead873bb839858d9bd7392281d1f02f41","after_hash":"248872e425efb9c9b636e85457091c050567a0d60e0ce8987f4f18d622a21c3f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version"